---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Navbar from '../../components/Navbar.astro';
import PageShell from '../../components/PageShell.astro';
---

<Layout 
    title="Medical Disclaimer | Real BMI"
    description="Review the Real BMI medical disclaimer. Our calculators offer educational health estimates based on WHO & CDC references and are not diagnostic tools."
    canonicalURL="https://realbmicalculator.com/en/disclaimer/"
>
    <Navbar />
    <PageShell
      title="Medical Disclaimer"
      eyebrow="Important health notice"
      description="Understand how Real BMI provides educational health estimates and why you should consult a qualified professional for medical decisions."
      returnUrl="/en/"
      returnLabel="Home"
    >
      <div class="space-y-8 prose prose-zinc dark:prose-invert max-w-none text-[var(--muted-foreground)] leading-relaxed text-base sm:text-lg font-medium opacity-90">
        
        <p class="text-lg sm:text-xl font-normal text-[var(--foreground)] leading-relaxed">
          The computational tools, interactive charts, and health information provided by <strong>Real BMI</strong> are designed strictly for educational, informational, and personal awareness purposes.
        </p>

        <!-- 1. What Real BMI Is -->
        <div class="space-y-2">
          <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase tracking-tight text-[var(--foreground)]">
            What Real BMI Is
          </h2>
          <p>
            Real BMI is a free, evidence-based digital health screening suite. We provide:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1.5">
            <li>Mathematical estimates based on published scientific formulas and international public health guidelines (such as the WHO, CDC, and NIH).</li>
            <li>Interactive body volume and mass visualizers for educational conceptualization.</li>
            <li>General population reference ranges to help you understand common biometric benchmarks.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- 2. What Real BMI Is Not -->
        <div class="space-y-2">
          <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase tracking-tight text-[var(--foreground)]">
            What Real BMI Is Not
          </h2>
          <p>
            Real BMI is not a licensed medical provider and does not offer clinical services:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1.5">
            <li><strong>Not Medical Advice:</strong> Our outputs do not constitute professional medical advice, formal clinical diagnosis, or individualized treatment plans.</li>
            <li><strong>Not a Diagnostic Tool:</strong> A calculator result cannot detect, diagnose, or rule out underlying cardiometabolic conditions, hormonal imbalances, or nutritional deficiencies.</li>
            <li><strong>Not a Prescriptive Guide:</strong> You should never start or stop medications, or undertake severe calorie restriction or extreme exercise programs based solely on calculator scores.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- 3. Who Should Consult a Doctor -->
        <div class="space-y-2">
          <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase tracking-tight text-[var(--foreground)]">
            Who Should Consult a Doctor
          </h2>
          <p>
            We strongly advise discussing your health metrics with a licensed physician, registered dietitian, or qualified healthcare provider, especially if you:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1.5">
            <li>Are planning significant weight loss, weight gain, or major dietary changes.</li>
            <li>Have existing chronic conditions such as diabetes, hypertension, cardiovascular disease, or thyroid disorders.</li>
            <li>Are pregnant, lactating, or recovering from medical procedures.</li>
            <li>Have a personal history of eating disorders or body dysmorphia.</li>
            <li>Notice sudden, unexplained fluctuations in body weight.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- 4. Emergency Situations (Callout Box) -->
        <div class="p-5 sm:p-6 rounded-2xl bg-amber-500/10 border border-amber-500/30 text-[var(--foreground)] space-y-2 not-prose">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-amber-600 dark:text-amber-400 font-display font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-xs sm:text-sm">
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 shrink-0" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M12 9v2m0 4h.01m-6.938 4h13.856c1.54 0 2.502-1.667 1.732-3L13.732 4c-.77-1.333-2.694-1.333-3.464 0L3.34 16c-.77 1.333.192 3 1.732 3z"/>
            </svg>
            Emergency Situations
          </div>
          <h3 class="text-base sm:text-lg font-bold text-[var(--foreground)]">
            Immediate Medical Assistance
          </h3>
          <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted-foreground)] font-medium">
            Real BMI is not designed for acute or emergency medical care. If you are experiencing chest pain, shortness of breath, sudden dizziness, acute weakness, or any life-threatening symptoms, immediately call your local emergency medical services (such as 911 in the US, 112 in Europe/India, or local emergency number) or proceed to the nearest hospital emergency department.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- 5. BMI Limitations -->
        <div class="space-y-2">
          <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase tracking-tight text-[var(--foreground)]">
            BMI Limitations
          </h2>
          <p>
            Standard Body Mass Index (BMI) has recognized epidemiological and physiological limitations:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1.5">
            <li><strong>Body Composition:</strong> BMI calculates weight relative to height squared (kg/m²), but cannot distinguish between lean muscle mass, bone density, and visceral fat. Muscular athletes often register an 'overweight' BMI despite maintaining very low body fat.</li>
            <li><strong>Age & Sarcopenia:</strong> Older adults naturally lose skeletal muscle (sarcopenia), which can mask elevated visceral fat under a 'normal' BMI score.</li>
            <li><strong>Ethnic Variance:</strong> Visceral fat distribution and cardiometabolic risks vary across populations. For instance, WHO expert consultations established lower public health thresholds for Asian populations (23.0 kg/m² vs 25.0 kg/m²).</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- 6. Privacy: No Personal Health Information Stored -->
        <div class="space-y-2">
          <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase tracking-tight text-[var(--foreground)]">
            Privacy: No Personal Health Information Stored
          </h2>
          <p>
            Your health numbers belong solely to you:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1.5">
            <li><strong>Client-Side Processing:</strong> All calculations run directly inside your web browser using local JavaScript.</li>
            <li><strong>No Storage or Tracking:</strong> We do not collect, store, transmit, or share your height, weight, age, waist measurements, or calculated health outcomes on our servers.</li>
            <li><strong>Zero Public Records:</strong> Real BMI does not host public message boards, member directories, or user profiles where personal data could ever be exposed.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- 7. Legal Disclaimer -->
        <div class="space-y-2">
          <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase tracking-tight text-[var(--foreground)]">
            Legal Disclaimer & Limitation of Liability
          </h2>
          <p>
            Neither Real BMI, its creators, nor contributing authors assume any legal liability or responsibility for decisions, dietary choices, or health outcomes resulting from the use of our calculators or website content. By using Real BMI, you acknowledge and agree that your engagement with our calculators is undertaken voluntarily and at your own sole discretion.
          </p>
        </div>

      </div>
    </PageShell>
</Layout>
